9 2 "// py-mp-1125: Go's runtime unblocks the signals it must see (SIGINT, SIGTERM, SIGHUP, SIGUSR1 and the rest of its"] [160 2 "// table's kill and throw signals) on every thread at its start, so a mask inherited with them blocked is lost before"] [161 2 "// this init; bin/pyi python reads the mask of its shell (/proc/PID/status' SigBlk, the one the executable is started"] [162 2 "// with) into PYI_START_SIGBLK. Such a signal is blocked here too and notified to the module, so one that arrives"] [163 2 "// before the program unblocks it is held (sigpending) and not the death of Go's default action: resource_tracker's"] [164 2 "// SIGINT and SIGTERM, blocked by its parent from the spawn to its main's SIG_IGN. Not the synchronous faults, SIGURG"] [165 2 "// (Go's preemption) or SIGPROF; the variable is the start's, so no child inherits it."] [167 70 "// pending at the exec (bin/pyi discarded them)"] [188 1 "// writeInterruptible is os.write's write to a blocking pipe, as write(2) is under CPython's handlers (no SA_RESTART: a"] [189 1 "// signal interrupts it, os.write's PyErr_CheckSignals runs the handlers, PEP 475's retry; py-mods-1122, test_io's"] [190 1 "// SignalsTest.test_interrupted_write_*, which hung): in the main thread, a FIFO's write (a regular file's never blocks;"] [191 1 "// sockets write by socket's own calls) waits for room by ppoll with the wake pipe (the GIL released, the handlers run when"] [192 1 "// a signal arrives) and writes at most PIPE_BUF bytes at a time, which a pipe that polls writable takes without blocking"] [193 1 "// (no flag of the shared file description changed), until every byte is written; a handler that raises ends it with its"] [194 1 "// exception (CPython's partial count, then the handler's exception at the next check), one that returns lets it go on."] [195 1 "// handled false: not such a write (another thread, a non-blocking descriptor, no FIFO, nothing to write), written as"] [196 1 "// before."] [209 23 "// PIPE_BUF: a pipe that polls writable has at least this much room"]] :go/pos {:name [3 9] :package [3 1]} :go/semis [[99 40] [105 39] [117 33] [129 48] [135 35] [151 91] [154 12] [154 22] [166 39] [170 44] [171 14] [171 24] [214 35]]} (go/file "builtins_signal_wait.go" :build ["//go:build linux"] :imports [


